From 33984948b0ead6a9edd85a7e398aa3eed363d517 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 21:59:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] FEX: draw probe on its own device and thread

The fex23 draw probe ran inside device creation on the game's own
Vulkan device and queue, in one submission, and D2R crashed at start.
Now the probe runs on its own thread, 2 s after the device is made
(VKD3D_FEX_DRAW_PROBE_DELAY), on a Vulkan device of its own, so a GPU
fault in the probe loses only that device. Each test is its own
submission and is named in the gpu report ('  draw probe: test N of 12
running') 1.5 s before it is sent, so a crash shows which test it was.
A failing test stops the probe; the note gives the tests done so far
and where it stopped. The result note goes out from report 31 on.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WZVGoVEaHJ78mpf2D3MiER
